  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough next Tuesday...\n\nA series of weak shortwaves embedded in SW flow aloft, combined\nwith elevated monsoon moisture, will continue to bring a daily \nrisk (10-30% chance) of thunderstorms each day through Friday. \nThere is a slight risk of severe storms in far southeast MT today,\nmainly east of Rosebud County between 1-6pm. Strong wind gusts is\nthe main risk but pwats are quite high and thus locally heavy \nrain can be expected, and there may be enough instability/shear to\nsupport marginally severe hail. Higher based storms capable of \nproducing gusty winds will impact western and central portions of \nour cwa. A similar story is expected with convection Thursday & \nFriday, and greatest coverage of storms should continue to exist \nin our east. Skies will remain hazy through the period as we \nadvect lofted smoke from the numerous wildfires in OR/WA.\n\nSaturday is hotter & drier as monsoon moisture is finally scoured\nout of the northern great basin. With 700mb temps of +18C to +20C\nwe are looking at another day of extreme heat with highs well over\n100F. Daily records for Aug 1st are definitely breakable, and \nwould not be surprised to see notoriously hot locations reach 110F\n(smoke permitting) for the 2nd time this summer. If you have \noutdoor activities planned Saturday please protect yourself from \nthe heat. Regarding fire weather, mixed winds will be breezy at \ntimes, but mid level flow on the order of 10-20kts does not \nsupport strong winds. Furthermore, a cold front looks to arrive \nafter 06Z Saturday night. All told, Saturday will see elevated \nfire wx concerns but frontal timing seems late enough to prevent \nit from being a more problematic day. Will need to monitor this.\n\nThe initial cold front Saturday night will be followed by another\nstronger front Sunday night, associated with a sharper trof\nskirting across the MT/Canada border. Each of these fronts look\ndry for us, but we will see much cooler temps by Monday & Tuesday\nwith highs in the upper 70s & 80s. The chances of precip are low \non these days. \n\nFinally, with regard to smoke, the frontal passages Saturday night\nand Sunday night could be followed by increased surface smoke per\nthe subsidence and developing upslope winds. This will need to be\nwatched.\n\nJKL",
